faq:
  - q: Can we keep stock in more than one place?
    a: Yes. Create warehouses for the main store, branches, sites and vehicles, and transfer stock between them. Each transfer is recorded as a movement out and a movement in.
  - q: How is material issued to a project?
    a: The store issues a quantity from a chosen warehouse to a project. The movement is recorded in the ledger with the project reference, and returns are recorded the same way.
  - q: Do we get a low stock alert?
    a: Yes. Each item has a reorder level, and users see a low stock alert when available quantity falls to that level. Reserved stock is excluded from availability.
  - q: Is the quotation linked to the catalogue?
    a: Yes. The quotation bill of materials is built from the same catalogue using quantity rules per item, so prices and item names match what the store holds.
  - q: Can we record supplier purchases?
    a: Yes. Supplier quotes, purchase orders and tax invoices can be recorded with GST by line, and received stock goes into the chosen warehouse.
